1
00:02:03,140 --> 00:02:04,710
Have some hot tea.

2
00:02:06,870 --> 00:02:09,020
Oh, and... where is Pim?

3
00:02:23,760 --> 00:02:24,670
Thank you.

4
00:02:33,200 --> 00:02:36,600
Well then, I'll take my leave.

5
00:02:37,140 --> 00:02:38,600
So you two can talk comfortably.

6
00:02:40,450 --> 00:02:41,560
Excuse me, Mr.Phong.

7
00:03:00,020 --> 00:03:04,350
I am truly sorry for speaking so harshly to you and insulting you,

8
00:03:06,210 --> 00:03:10,060
even though I was the one who misunderstood

9
00:03:10,790 --> 00:03:12,360
and never bothered to listen to anyone.

10
00:03:18,530 --> 00:03:19,860
I was wrong.

11
00:03:41,750 --> 00:03:42,630
Calm down, dear.

12
00:03:52,520 --> 00:03:54,280
Don't give in too easily, Pim.

13
00:04:10,380 --> 00:04:11,630
Are you finished with what you needed to do?

14
00:04:12,370 --> 00:04:13,170
Please leave.

15
00:04:13,680 --> 00:04:14,810
Oh...  Pim.

16
00:04:21,290 --> 00:04:22,810
I'm not someone you can just mess with.

17
00:04:23,860 --> 00:04:27,070
I could still somewhat accept it when you insulted me based on a misunderstanding.

18
00:04:27,530 --> 00:04:29,060
But this time, you insulted my dad,

19
00:04:29,540 --> 00:04:30,920
the person who raised me so well.

20
00:04:31,180 --> 00:04:32,580
That’s going a bit too far.

21
00:04:35,380 --> 00:04:37,190
I truly didn't mean to.

22
00:04:37,890 --> 00:04:39,010
I'm so sorry.

23
00:04:40,280 --> 00:04:41,620
If you were in my shoes,

24
00:04:42,770 --> 00:04:44,360
you would have misunderstood too.

25
00:04:46,890 --> 00:04:48,550
I can go swear an oath anywhere,

26
00:04:49,940 --> 00:04:51,440
I really didn't mean to.

27
00:04:52,500 --> 00:04:53,930
Please give me a second chance.

28
00:04:56,860 --> 00:04:58,060
That's easy to say.

29
00:04:59,550 --> 00:05:02,650
Even without meaning to, you were able to insult my dad like that.

30
00:05:04,650 --> 00:05:06,650
You apologize just so others will forgive you,

31
00:05:07,040 --> 00:05:08,550
and once you feel better, it's over.

32
00:05:09,650 --> 00:05:11,530
But what about my feelings that were hurt?

33
00:05:12,240 --> 00:05:13,480
How are you going to fix that?

34
00:05:26,640 --> 00:05:28,860
I know that you want to apologize,

35
00:05:29,650 --> 00:05:31,480
but don't expect me to forgive you.

36
00:05:33,590 --> 00:05:34,470
Ms. Pim,

37
00:05:35,260 --> 00:05:36,030
Ms. Pim!

38
00:05:53,409 --> 00:05:54,310
I'm sorry,

39
00:05:55,920 --> 00:05:59,590
I realize now that I spoke way too harshly.

40
00:06:11,220 --> 00:06:12,280
What on earth are you doing?

41
00:06:28,020 --> 00:06:32,409
I know that no matter how many times I apologize,

42
00:06:34,360 --> 00:06:36,140
you probably won't forgive me.

43
00:06:41,140 --> 00:06:42,560
You don't have to go this far.

44
00:06:42,870 --> 00:06:43,900
I'm not that important.

45
00:07:02,920 --> 00:07:03,890
That's not true at all,

46
00:07:05,470 --> 00:07:07,110
You are important to me.

47
00:07:08,740 --> 00:07:09,930
If it were anyone else,

48
00:07:12,450 --> 00:07:13,850
I wouldn't go to this length.

49
00:07:24,680 --> 00:07:26,010
I'm truly sorry for insulting you

50
00:07:27,460 --> 00:07:29,670
and your father so harshly.

51
00:07:36,659 --> 00:07:38,240
The reason I did all that is...

52
00:07:43,380 --> 00:07:44,830
because I love you.

53
00:08:17,060 --> 00:08:18,050
Ms. Pim...

54
00:08:22,890 --> 00:08:24,500
could you please give me another chance?

55
00:08:27,310 --> 00:08:28,670
Let me love you

56
00:08:31,630 --> 00:08:32,860
the way I want to love you.

57
00:09:48,410 --> 00:09:50,320
Dad, you aren't mad at me, right?

58
00:09:52,900 --> 00:09:54,970
How could I be mad at you?

59
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:57,390
It’s your life, so of course you have to choose for yourself.

60
00:09:58,210 --> 00:10:01,910
You are really mad at me. But Kie...

61
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:03,110
She curses at me!

62
00:10:03,620 --> 00:10:05,240
Doesn't have a job,

63
00:10:05,270 --> 00:10:06,790
spends all day hanging around and having fun,

64
00:10:07,190 --> 00:10:09,320
and lives off the family fortune just to squander it.

65
00:10:10,900 --> 00:10:14,220
And from what angle do you expect me to look at her with affection, my dear? Hmm?

66
00:10:17,970 --> 00:10:20,720
Dad, you make it sound like he doesn't have a single good quality.

67
00:10:22,420 --> 00:10:24,190
Maybe she does,

68
00:10:25,110 --> 00:10:31,170
but it must be sooooo deep down that I just can't see it.

69
00:10:33,670 --> 00:10:34,900
But you can see it, right?

70
00:10:42,370 --> 00:10:45,550
Pim, I am just worried about you.

71
00:10:46,210 --> 00:10:49,650
If she makes you happy, I won't stand in the way.

72
00:10:52,800 --> 00:10:54,310
Thank you, Dad,

73
00:10:58,190 --> 00:10:59,660
for giving Kie a chance.

74
00:11:21,970 --> 00:11:23,340
Has Pim started dating you already?

75
00:11:25,160 --> 00:11:25,840
Yes.

76
00:11:26,840 --> 00:11:27,640
Yesterday?

77
00:11:29,140 --> 00:11:29,800
Yes.

78
00:11:30,130 --> 00:11:32,900
Seriously? After you just got into a huge fight with her dad?

79
00:11:34,550 --> 00:11:35,560
Yes.

80
00:11:41,010 --> 00:11:42,670
Are you sure you're not just imagining things?

81
00:11:42,700 --> 00:11:46,580
Hm... It's only been a few days since Pha's funeral.

82
00:11:47,080 --> 00:11:49,990
Are you really sure your heart is ready for this, hmmm?

83
00:11:53,860 --> 00:11:57,270
I'm truly confident that Pim is the right one.

84
00:11:59,520 --> 00:12:02,740
She always says she’s confident with everyone like that.

85
00:12:04,220 --> 00:12:05,470
And then boom,

86
00:12:06,230 --> 00:12:07,250
total disaster.

87
00:12:11,090 --> 00:12:12,720
I'm genuinely confident about this one.

88
00:12:14,750 --> 00:12:16,040
Pim...

89
00:12:17,520 --> 00:12:19,020
she isn't like anyone I've been with before.

90
00:12:20,300 --> 00:12:22,230
You said the exact same thing about Pha, you know.

91
00:12:24,990 --> 00:12:27,400
If I say I'm confident, then I'm confident, Mom.

92
00:12:31,360 --> 00:12:34,870
And you two, is there anything else you want to surprise me with? Hmm?

93
00:12:35,130 --> 00:12:36,950
I'd rather you just shock me all at once.

94
00:12:38,800 --> 00:12:40,360
No, there isn't.

95
00:12:41,240 --> 00:12:45,280
The only thing I will marry is my career.

96
00:12:45,320 --> 00:12:48,370
Oh, I completely forgot.

97
00:12:48,410 --> 00:12:50,090
I need to get back to work, Mom.

98
00:12:57,850 --> 00:12:58,760
No, Mom.

99
00:12:59,190 --> 00:13:02,230
The closest my heart gets to anything is just these patients.

100
00:13:03,000 --> 00:13:05,060
All day long it's just cases to treat, needles,

101
00:13:05,090 --> 00:13:07,400
and bandages.

102
00:13:07,430 --> 00:13:09,090
That's already enough for me.

103
00:13:09,820 --> 00:13:11,080
I've got to run to my shift now.

104
00:13:11,480 --> 00:13:12,130
Okay, dear.

105
00:13:25,130 --> 00:13:27,270
Mom, I really love this person.

106
00:13:46,360 --> 00:13:47,390
Examine me, please.

107
00:13:50,260 --> 00:13:50,700
No.

108
00:13:52,300 --> 00:13:53,290
Examine me!

109
00:13:54,410 --> 00:13:56,150
There are so many other doctors.

110
00:13:56,250 --> 00:13:57,880
Why do I have to be the one to examine you?

111
00:14:04,450 --> 00:14:07,460
Because you've been treating me from the very beginning.

112
00:14:08,030 --> 00:14:12,550
Who else knows my case as well as you do, right?

113
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:21,720
Kids will be kids. always so stubborn.

114
00:14:27,380 --> 00:14:28,650
I'm not a kid. Fine,

115
00:14:29,780 --> 00:14:31,050
I won't have you examine them.

116
00:14:48,610 --> 00:14:51,720
Alright, alright, I'll examine you, patient.

117
00:16:13,870 --> 00:16:17,550
So, aren't you interested in my brother at all?

118
00:16:18,370 --> 00:16:21,680
P’Siva is so handsome, rich,

119
00:16:21,950 --> 00:16:23,400
and completely perfect.

120
00:16:26,390 --> 00:16:29,990
Is that why you wanted me to examine you over, just to ask about this?

121
00:16:35,120 --> 00:16:35,640
Yes?

122
00:16:40,330 --> 00:16:42,840
I'm just curious.

123
00:16:44,750 --> 00:16:46,410
There's nothing complicated about it.

124
00:16:47,040 --> 00:16:48,070
I simply don't love him.

125
00:16:48,950 --> 00:16:51,230
P’Siva is a great senior

126
00:16:51,950 --> 00:16:53,380
and a good friend,

127
00:16:54,150 --> 00:16:56,310
but that's all he'll ever be.

128
00:17:06,240 --> 00:17:11,329
Oh, I'm still hurting here.

129
00:17:12,530 --> 00:17:15,190
Can you be a bit more thorough with the examination,

130
00:17:20,770 --> 00:17:21,240
please?

131
00:17:59,730 --> 00:18:07,780
In that case, can you be my personal doctor from now on?

132
00:18:16,480 --> 00:18:21,130
If you want to examine with me, make sure you book your appointment properly.

133
00:19:53,440 --> 00:19:54,470
Everything is set.

134
00:19:54,970 --> 00:19:58,230
If there's anything else, I'll contact you back.

135
00:20:00,710 --> 00:20:06,460
Do you have any errands to run next?

136
00:20:08,450 --> 00:20:09,400
Is there something you want?

137
00:20:12,030 --> 00:20:13,110
There's nothing.

138
00:20:13,590 --> 00:20:17,540
I was just going to invite you to go eat.

139
00:20:22,750 --> 00:20:24,400
I don't have any business to attend to.

140
00:20:45,440 --> 00:20:46,830
I'm sorry,

141
00:20:47,580 --> 00:20:48,980
my partner just arrived to pick me up.

142
00:20:49,680 --> 00:20:50,810
I must be going now.

143
00:21:15,080 --> 00:21:16,870
Why didn't you wait in the car?

144
00:21:17,320 --> 00:21:18,870
I wanted to see you sooner.

145
00:21:20,840 --> 00:21:23,690
Kie, please don't do that.

146
00:21:30,090 --> 00:21:32,700
Before heading home, shall we stop by to grab something to eat?

147
00:21:33,160 --> 00:21:34,200
Are you hungry?

148
00:21:35,060 --> 00:21:38,520
Well, that depends on what kind of "hungry" you mean.

149
00:21:40,620 --> 00:21:41,830
Be serious.

150
00:21:42,120 --> 00:21:44,810
If you're going to invite me to eat, do you already have a restaurant in mind?

151
00:21:45,660 --> 00:21:46,910
Not yet.

152
00:21:47,360 --> 00:21:48,570
It's totally up to you.

153
00:21:50,930 --> 00:21:53,720
Don't blame me later, then.

154
00:22:26,130 --> 00:22:27,190
Isn't it delicious?

155
00:22:30,090 --> 00:22:32,680
No, it is delicious.

156
00:22:33,380 --> 00:22:36,560
I was just thinking that you're pretty chill.

157
00:22:38,350 --> 00:22:39,670
That's not unusual.

158
00:22:40,060 --> 00:22:42,520
This place is way better than the ones in the mall.

159
00:22:44,210 --> 00:22:45,030
True.

160
00:22:46,430 --> 00:22:49,640
But I don't usually meet people like you.

161
00:22:55,050 --> 00:22:56,910
Oh, I mean,

162
00:22:57,930 --> 00:23:02,170
other people usually like me to take them to fine dining, omakase,

163
00:23:02,660 --> 00:23:04,660
or chef's tables.

164
00:23:06,490 --> 00:23:09,270
No way, those are expensive.

165
00:23:14,050 --> 00:23:15,480
Did I say something wrong?

166
00:23:15,790 --> 00:23:16,910
Not at all.

167
00:23:18,170 --> 00:23:21,010
Sometimes I think those things are way too expensive, too.

168
00:23:25,780 --> 00:23:29,430
So what do you actually like to eat?

169
00:23:31,630 --> 00:23:33,130
I can eat anything,

170
00:23:33,760 --> 00:23:35,020
as long as it's delicious.

171
00:23:37,300 --> 00:23:40,970
Hearing that makes me a little less stressed.

172
00:23:42,960 --> 00:23:44,210
What do you mean?

173
00:23:45,170 --> 00:23:51,130
Did you think I was some spoiled rich girl who only eats over-priced food?

174
00:23:54,460 --> 00:23:54,910
Yes.

175
00:23:56,090 --> 00:23:57,250
Ms. Pim,

176
00:23:59,490 --> 00:24:04,770
How about we go for a walk at the market after we finish eating?

177
00:24:06,120 --> 00:24:11,260
That way, you will see that I'm not some spoiled rich girl who only eats at fancy department stores.

178
00:26:28,390 --> 00:26:30,510
I haven't seen you paint in a long time.

179
00:26:31,440 --> 00:26:32,620
What inspired you?

180
00:26:34,060 --> 00:26:35,080
Nothing really,

181
00:26:36,110 --> 00:26:36,920
I just wanted to.

182
00:26:38,610 --> 00:26:41,440
Ms. Pim is quite something, too.

183
00:26:43,690 --> 00:26:44,890
I told you already,

184
00:26:46,560 --> 00:26:49,450
Khun Pim is the right one.

185
00:26:58,480 --> 00:27:06,810
I finally understand the difference between being in love and just being infatuated.

186
00:28:25,110 --> 00:28:26,230
Here's some water, Ms. Kaew.

187
00:28:27,380 --> 00:28:28,540
Thank you, Ms. Pim.

188
00:28:29,460 --> 00:28:30,020
Oh...

189
00:28:35,440 --> 00:28:37,150
here is the pen you left behind, Ms. Pim.

190
00:28:38,530 --> 00:28:39,500
Thank you.

191
00:28:43,540 --> 00:28:44,910
Are you okay, Ms. Kaew?

192
00:28:45,510 --> 00:28:46,810
You look very pale.

193
00:28:49,520 --> 00:28:50,390
I'm fine.

194
00:28:51,330 --> 00:28:52,670
I just got carsick,

195
00:28:53,550 --> 00:28:54,390
it'll pass soon.

196
00:28:59,060 --> 00:29:00,090
This way, Ms. Kaew.

197
00:29:00,120 --> 00:29:01,250
I'll take you to the restroom.

198
00:29:08,870 --> 00:29:10,440
Have a seat and rest here.

199
00:29:10,920 --> 00:29:12,210
I'll go get some medicine for you.

200
00:29:12,900 --> 00:29:14,220
Thank you so much.

201
00:30:00,360 --> 00:30:01,420
I love you, Pim.

202
00:30:02,920 --> 00:30:03,740
Goodnight!

203
00:30:17,580 --> 00:30:20,490
Why that face? Is there something you want to tell me?

204
00:30:22,580 --> 00:30:23,480
Ummmm.

205
00:30:24,760 --> 00:30:27,800
You're no longer friends with P'Kaew on SNS anymore, right?

206
00:30:29,380 --> 00:30:31,750
Who would ever want to be friends with an asshole like that?

207
00:30:34,910 --> 00:30:36,200
Then don't look.

208
00:30:37,040 --> 00:30:37,800
Look at what?

209
00:30:38,420 --> 00:30:39,590
Give it here and let me see right now.

210
00:30:40,660 --> 00:30:43,750
Vodka, stop stalling.

211
00:30:49,640 --> 00:30:52,230
Wait... this is Pim's house!

212
00:30:54,540 --> 00:30:56,010
Did you see the caption?

213
00:30:56,790 --> 00:30:58,410
"New love."

214
00:31:16,210 --> 00:31:18,840
Go throw a huge fit at Pim,

215
00:31:19,080 --> 00:31:21,050
so she can see your true colors sooner

216
00:31:21,890 --> 00:31:23,350
and finally break up with you.

217
00:31:35,560 --> 00:31:36,710
Kie, Kie, Kie,

218
00:31:37,050 --> 00:31:39,130
calm down first, Kie.

219
00:31:43,010 --> 00:31:45,270
Kie, have you thought this through carefully?

220
00:31:46,420 --> 00:31:47,510
Yeah,  P’Kie.

221
00:31:47,840 --> 00:31:50,930
If you lose your temper with Ms. Pim, you’ll just be playing right into P’Kaew's hands.

222
00:31:51,370 --> 00:31:52,230
I know already.

223
00:31:52,810 --> 00:31:55,160
I’m not stupid enough to let Kaew push my buttons so easily.

224
00:31:56,450 --> 00:31:58,780
Kaew probably wants to steal Pim away from me.

225
00:32:00,720 --> 00:32:05,320
She probably doesn’t realize I know she's the one managing the project Pim applied to get a loan for.

226
00:32:06,230 --> 00:32:07,090
But you know...

227
00:32:07,560 --> 00:32:08,690
How did you find out?

228
00:32:09,040 --> 00:32:10,220
It wasn't hard at all.

229
00:32:10,570 --> 00:32:13,910
I just had Nuan look into it, that's all.

230
00:32:14,800 --> 00:32:17,600
Now that you know this, why are you going to see Ms. Pim?

231
00:32:42,120 --> 00:32:43,080
Ms. Pim.

232
00:32:45,670 --> 00:32:47,660
Kie, what brings you here so early in the morning?

233
00:32:48,490 --> 00:32:50,970
Well, aren't you going to work in Hua Hin today?

234
00:32:52,900 --> 00:32:54,440
I want to take you there.

235
00:32:55,280 --> 00:32:56,430
Let me carry your things for you.

236
00:32:56,650 --> 00:32:57,930
That's alright, thank you.

237
00:32:57,970 --> 00:32:59,140
Please let me hold it.

238
00:32:59,400 --> 00:33:02,740
I want to take care of you the way a partner does.

239
00:33:05,100 --> 00:33:06,040
Okay.

240
00:33:09,110 --> 00:33:11,160
Come on, Kie will drive for you.

241
00:33:12,320 --> 00:33:12,690
Let's go.

242
00:33:24,390 --> 00:33:27,800
Kie, why are you covering my eyes?

243
00:33:28,400 --> 00:33:30,220
I have already been to your house before.

244
00:33:31,240 --> 00:33:32,680
Just humor me a little bit, okay?

245
00:33:33,320 --> 00:33:35,300
I just want to surprise you.

246
00:33:36,220 --> 00:33:37,250
A surprise?

247
00:33:40,270 --> 00:33:41,910
Yes. We're almost there.

248
00:33:44,350 --> 00:33:50,680
3 2 1 Surprise!

249
00:34:06,930 --> 00:34:08,760
Do you really have to go all out of this?

250
00:34:10,360 --> 00:34:11,969
I’m not going all out.

251
00:34:13,350 --> 00:34:16,870
I see that you work hard every day,

252
00:34:22,219 --> 00:34:24,520
So I wanted to do something nice for you.

253
00:34:34,130 --> 00:34:35,929
What happened to you?

254
00:34:36,650 --> 00:34:38,230
It wasn't like this this morning.

255
00:34:40,500 --> 00:34:43,560
Guess what I went and did.

256
00:34:52,020 --> 00:34:53,690
Did you cook this yourself?

257
00:34:55,600 --> 00:34:56,489
Yes, I did!

258
00:34:57,490 --> 00:35:00,760
But I got all the recipes from the internet.

259
00:35:01,840 --> 00:35:05,710
I'm not sure if it'll be to the liking of someone around here.

260
00:35:08,800 --> 00:35:13,020
Just knowing that you put in the effort makes me pleased enough.

261
00:35:15,140 --> 00:35:16,210
Thank you.

262
00:35:29,730 --> 00:35:31,290
Is that all the thanks I get?

263
00:37:13,400 --> 00:37:17,450
I think we should eat first, shall we?

264
00:37:18,750 --> 00:37:20,210
You put an effort into making this.

265
00:37:58,850 --> 00:38:04,680
Please don't dwell on what happened in the dining room just now.

266
00:38:06,620 --> 00:38:10,230
I just want us to take things slow.

267
00:38:13,910 --> 00:38:17,560
I'm sorry for being in such a rush.

268
00:38:20,440 --> 00:38:22,430
Did I startle you?

269
00:38:24,080 --> 00:38:25,210
A little bit,

270
00:38:26,850 --> 00:38:28,210
but...

271
00:38:31,300 --> 00:38:32,810
I'd rather not say.

272
00:38:49,970 --> 00:38:51,010
Why is that?

273
00:38:54,070 --> 00:38:58,470
Or... if we hadn't stopped there,

274
00:38:59,890 --> 00:39:02,220
would we have ended up having more than just dinner?

275
00:39:04,210 --> 00:39:08,210
What on earth are you saying?

276
00:39:10,880 --> 00:39:12,230
It's completely fine,

277
00:39:14,760 --> 00:39:15,850
I can wait.

278
00:39:22,790 --> 00:39:26,890
We can talk about it whenever you're ready.

279
00:39:36,990 --> 00:39:39,930
Thank you for understanding me.

280
00:39:41,820 --> 00:39:47,020
I just want to make sure we really feel the same way.

281
00:39:50,530 --> 00:39:55,490
I'll make sure you're certain that I truly love you.

282
00:39:59,610 --> 00:40:00,940
No need to rush.

283
00:40:02,870 --> 00:40:04,870
Pim is right here with you

284
00:40:05,480 --> 00:40:06,740
and isn't going anywhere, for sure.

285
00:40:10,060 --> 00:40:12,800
You promise you won't go away from me, right?

286
00:40:37,040 --> 00:40:37,590
Yes,

287
00:40:39,210 --> 00:40:40,330
I promises.

288
00:41:12,220 --> 00:41:15,450
Kie, you can't keep running down like this every morning.

289
00:41:15,920 --> 00:41:17,560
But I'm afraid I won't make it on time to pick up Pim.

290
00:41:17,940 --> 00:41:19,890
You've been doing this for a month already.

291
00:41:19,910 --> 00:41:21,200
How are you still not used to it?

292
00:41:22,720 --> 00:41:24,720
Well, I've never woken up early before.

293
00:41:25,650 --> 00:41:29,440
Ah, just like how you're trying to cut down on drinking alcohol ?

294
00:41:29,480 --> 00:41:30,790
Still not used to that either, huh?

295
00:41:32,460 --> 00:41:33,150
Vodka!

296
00:41:34,720 --> 00:41:36,200
Aren't you going to see Pim?

297
00:41:36,650 --> 00:41:37,950
Then hurry up and go.

298
00:41:38,170 --> 00:41:42,500
Standing here arguing with Vodka isn't going to make you any less late.

299
00:41:42,720 --> 00:41:43,330
True.

300
00:41:44,060 --> 00:41:44,760
I will leave, then!

301
00:42:48,110 --> 00:42:51,610
You wouldn't mind getting your hands dirty like this, would you?

302
00:42:53,110 --> 00:42:54,690
How could I possibly mind

303
00:42:55,890 --> 00:42:57,420
when you don't mind either?

304
00:42:59,330 --> 00:43:03,200
Whatever you want to do, I want to do it right along with you.

305
00:43:07,440 --> 00:43:09,130
Has anyone ever told you

306
00:43:10,380 --> 00:43:11,720
that you have a sweet tongue?

307
00:43:17,100 --> 00:43:18,220
Never.

308
00:43:19,290 --> 00:43:22,490
People only ever told me I had a foul mouth.

309
00:43:26,490 --> 00:43:28,220
But I don't want a foul mouth anymore,

310
00:43:29,440 --> 00:43:32,850
I just want to be the one with a sweet tongue for you and only you, Pim.

311
00:43:46,460 --> 00:43:47,240
Pim...

312
00:43:50,950 --> 00:43:52,410
ever since I met you,

313
00:43:56,080 --> 00:44:00,410
I've finally learned what true love feels like.

314
00:44:05,490 --> 00:44:11,430
But did you know that I've been married three times already?

315
00:44:16,610 --> 00:44:17,760
And every single time,

316
00:44:21,100 --> 00:44:22,710
it ended in betrayal

317
00:44:24,570 --> 00:44:26,010
and parting through death.

318
00:44:27,170 --> 00:44:28,220
Kie..

319
00:44:33,060 --> 00:44:34,840
You don't despise me, do you, Pim?

320
00:44:41,420 --> 00:44:42,940
I don't despise you,

321
00:44:44,400 --> 00:44:49,670
I know that when you love someone, you love them truly.

322
00:44:57,940 --> 00:44:59,080
Then...

323
00:45:18,530 --> 00:45:25,880
Pim, will you be my one and only true love and final love?

324
00:45:30,210 --> 00:45:31,430
Marry me.

325
00:45:56,450 --> 00:46:02,440
Being in a relationship and getting married are not the same thing.

326
00:46:05,160 --> 00:46:09,400
Besides, my life isn't all that independent either.

327
00:46:23,390 --> 00:46:29,490
Mom, please help talk to Pim's family for me, please, please!

328
00:46:29,540 --> 00:46:31,160
Don't try to charm me .

329
00:46:31,180 --> 00:46:34,810
Every time you come to see me, you give me a headache.

330
00:46:38,270 --> 00:46:40,760
Please, I'm begging you, Mom.

331
00:46:40,790 --> 00:46:43,350
Aren't you going to help this lovely daughter of yours?

332
00:46:44,520 --> 00:46:46,330
You know I've never been able to say no to you,

333
00:46:46,350 --> 00:46:48,210
that's why you turned out the way you are.

334
00:46:50,500 --> 00:46:53,120
But this isn't an easy matter, Kie.

335
00:46:53,450 --> 00:46:57,240
Pim's family side, well... They're an old aristocracy.

336
00:46:57,280 --> 00:46:58,510
I don't even want to start talking to them.

337
00:46:59,230 --> 00:47:02,230
If they are from an aristocratic family, isn't that a good thing?

338
00:47:02,670 --> 00:47:03,770
What is good about it?

339
00:47:04,230 --> 00:47:06,700
Those high-society types refuse to face reality.

340
00:47:07,440 --> 00:47:09,210
They almost wiped Phong out financially.

341
00:47:10,530 --> 00:47:12,020
I'm not someone you can just mess with.

342
00:47:12,380 --> 00:47:15,530
I could still somewhat accept it when you insulted me based on a misunderstanding.

343
00:47:15,990 --> 00:47:19,450
But this time, you insulted my dad, the person who raised me so well.

344
00:47:19,670 --> 00:47:20,780
That’s going a bit

345
00:47:21,660 --> 00:47:23,880
Oh, no wonder...

346
00:47:24,260 --> 00:47:27,450
Back then, that’s why Pim was so furious.

347
00:47:30,280 --> 00:47:32,810
Phong raised his child through such hard times, dear.

348
00:47:33,730 --> 00:47:36,570
But luckily, Phong is capable, so he managed to get back on his feet.

349
00:47:39,360 --> 00:47:41,360
Why does Pim still care so much, Mom?

350
00:47:41,920 --> 00:47:44,170
If it were me, I wouldn’t care anymore.

351
00:47:44,850 --> 00:47:47,200
Well, we aren't her, so it's easy for us to say that, right?

352
00:47:48,620 --> 00:47:50,230
Put yourself in someone else's shoes, dear.

353
00:47:50,330 --> 00:47:54,680
How could a parent and child ever truly cut ties with each other, right?

354
00:47:55,570 --> 00:47:59,010
So what should we do then?

355
00:47:59,360 --> 00:48:01,690
Pim is worried that if we rush the wedding,

356
00:48:02,000 --> 00:48:06,210
her mother's side will definitely make a scene and refuse to accept it, Mom.

357
00:48:08,150 --> 00:48:10,140
It’s not like there’s no way out at all.

358
00:48:16,740 --> 00:48:18,960
Hey.. Who said you could leave!

359
00:48:20,320 --> 00:48:21,320
That’s enough, Da.

360
00:48:21,360 --> 00:48:22,950
Even a dog knows how to show gratitude,

361
00:48:22,970 --> 00:48:24,410
but raising a leech, this is what you get.

362
00:48:24,560 --> 00:48:25,410
Damn..

363
00:48:25,450 --> 00:48:27,030
Da, stop it!

364
00:48:27,070 --> 00:48:28,650
Calm down,

365
00:48:28,880 --> 00:48:30,210
we don't have many valuables left as it is.

366
00:48:42,990 --> 00:48:44,840
Twenty million. Is that enough?

367
00:48:45,810 --> 00:48:46,270
Pardon?

368
00:48:47,000 --> 00:48:48,260
For the dowry.

369
00:48:49,530 --> 00:48:52,680
I figured you wouldn't agree to this.

370
00:48:52,920 --> 00:48:56,230
Twenty million, upfront right here and now.

371
00:48:56,880 --> 00:48:58,520
But there's a condition.

372
00:48:59,530 --> 00:49:06,600
you and your daughter must promise not to disrupt the wedding between my niece and your niece.

373
00:49:07,460 --> 00:49:08,230
Deal?

374
00:49:08,800 --> 00:49:09,720
Just take it, Mom.

375
00:49:09,740 --> 00:49:11,350
I still have debts to pay off.

376
00:49:11,560 --> 00:49:13,760
Why are you like this?

377
00:49:14,070 --> 00:49:15,870
Getting all worked up over such a tiny amount of money.

378
00:49:16,080 --> 00:49:17,590
We aren't trashy low-lifes, you know.

379
00:49:17,860 --> 00:49:19,450
Low-life or not, I don't care.

380
00:49:19,740 --> 00:49:21,050
If you don't want it, Mom, I'll take it.

381
00:49:36,460 --> 00:49:37,920
Thank you so much, Grandpa.

382
00:49:37,960 --> 00:49:40,990
If you didn’t help me, I definitely wouldn't have made it.

383
00:49:44,700 --> 00:49:46,200
Don't overthink it.

384
00:49:46,790 --> 00:49:51,670
What I gave them was just a tiny bit of bank interest anyway.

385
00:49:52,150 --> 00:49:54,140
It won't even make a dent in my pocket.

386
00:49:54,900 --> 00:49:56,660
I love you the most!

387
00:49:57,730 --> 00:49:59,290
See? This is what happens when you spoil your granddaughter like this.

388
00:49:59,330 --> 00:50:01,520
That's why Kie has gone completely wild.

389
00:50:02,850 --> 00:50:06,780
If a small thing like this can buy happiness for my granddaughter,

390
00:50:07,240 --> 00:50:09,250
I'd willingly give even more.

391
00:50:10,160 --> 00:50:12,640
She really is your favorite granddaughter.

392
00:50:12,680 --> 00:50:14,730
Look at that, whatever she does,

393
00:50:14,760 --> 00:50:16,460
you approve of everything and side with her all the way.

394
00:50:19,280 --> 00:50:22,960
Hey, I only did this because I believed you, too.

395
00:50:23,000 --> 00:50:27,990
Didn't you say that thisPim is a genuinely good person?

396
00:50:37,030 --> 00:50:37,930
She’s here!

397
00:51:27,770 --> 00:51:30,520
Kie really has a sharp eye.

398
00:51:32,340 --> 00:51:34,950
Dad, does that mean Kie was blind all pass time?

399
00:51:36,220 --> 00:51:38,390
You said that yourself, I didn't.

400
00:51:38,910 --> 00:51:43,560
This is the person who is going to help Kie change for the better.

401
00:51:46,130 --> 00:51:48,010
Well, if she can change, that would be great.

402
00:51:48,620 --> 00:51:51,050
Maybe she'll finally be a good person.

403
00:51:51,320 --> 00:51:53,800
This time, it feels like God has taken pity on us.

404
00:51:56,200 --> 00:51:57,360
Oh, come on.

405
00:51:58,010 --> 00:52:01,480
Kie isn't that terrible.

406
00:52:01,750 --> 00:52:03,270
Sure, she can be self-indulgent sometimes,

407
00:52:03,570 --> 00:52:06,340
but when it comes to business acumen and quick-wittedness

408
00:52:07,090 --> 00:52:10,390
My granddaughter never loses to anyone.

409
00:52:11,690 --> 00:52:13,110
I don't believe it.

410
00:52:13,160 --> 00:52:17,010
You love and spoil Kie so much that you're completely blind to the fact

411
00:52:17,050 --> 00:52:19,190
that she just causes trouble every single day.

412
00:52:19,950 --> 00:52:23,750
Kie was lacking love, so she kept chasing after it.

413
00:52:24,820 --> 00:52:27,270
But now she has found it.

414
00:52:28,040 --> 00:52:34,870
Or do you not believe that good love can bring out the best version of someone?

415
00:52:50,330 --> 00:52:51,720
I would like to invite you as well.

416
00:53:01,460 --> 00:53:03,140
You have helped me out quite a lot.

417
00:53:07,740 --> 00:53:11,130
I was just doing my job.

418
00:53:13,780 --> 00:53:15,780
Anyway, congratulations!

419
00:53:17,860 --> 00:53:18,810
Thank you.

420
00:53:24,360 --> 00:53:25,570
I'll leave now.

421
00:53:44,580 --> 00:53:47,010
Ms. Pim, Ms. Pim

422
00:53:48,250 --> 00:53:49,450
Pim.

423
00:54:00,600 --> 00:54:03,290
Kie, we're in front of other people.

424
00:54:03,980 --> 00:54:05,030
Why?

425
00:54:05,350 --> 00:54:07,770
I was just missing my soon-to-be bride.

426
00:54:09,000 --> 00:54:11,640
Aren't you embarrassed saying things like that?

427
00:54:12,230 --> 00:54:14,020
I'm in love, why would I be embarrassed?

428
00:54:15,140 --> 00:54:19,210
I want to tell the whole world that I love you so much

429
00:54:20,170 --> 00:54:22,400
that no one else could ever take you away from me.

430
00:54:26,940 --> 00:54:30,320
I apologize for my fiancé, she tends to talk aimlessly.

431
00:54:32,940 --> 00:54:34,050
Wait for me a second, Kie.

432
00:54:34,210 --> 00:54:35,550
I'm going to run to the restroom.

433
00:54:35,570 --> 00:54:36,360
Sure.

434
00:54:36,850 --> 00:54:38,080
You guys can talk.

435
00:55:05,040 --> 00:55:06,010
What the hell are you smiling about?

436
00:55:06,300 --> 00:55:07,320
Are you crazy?

437
00:55:07,720 --> 00:55:08,480
Nothing.

438
00:55:09,460 --> 00:55:10,750
I just pity you.

439
00:55:11,880 --> 00:55:14,800
Do you really think something like that could make me break up with Pim?

440
00:55:16,630 --> 00:55:17,650
I'm not breaking up with her,

441
00:55:18,140 --> 00:55:19,910
and I'm going to marry her.

442
00:55:21,940 --> 00:55:22,980
Go ahead and marry her, then.

443
00:55:23,310 --> 00:55:24,980
You've already married three times anyway,

444
00:55:25,270 --> 00:55:26,870
what's a fourth time going to hurt?

445
00:55:27,980 --> 00:55:32,600
Oh... but I actually feel sorry for Ms. Pim.

446
00:55:33,370 --> 00:55:34,020
She's going to die…

447
00:55:34,050 --> 00:55:36,580
Bitch, don't you dare run your mouth and curse her!

448
00:55:37,160 --> 00:55:38,060
I'm not cursing her.

449
00:55:38,360 --> 00:55:40,250
You're the real jinx here,

450
00:55:40,280 --> 00:55:41,430
a spouse-eater.

451
00:55:42,350 --> 00:55:44,230
This time is different from all the others.

452
00:55:44,870 --> 00:55:46,470
I'm going to register our marriage with Pim.

453
00:55:48,760 --> 00:55:51,320
I've found someone worthy of registering a marriage with.

454
00:55:52,050 --> 00:55:53,710
Go ahead and stay hung up on the past.

455
00:55:54,170 --> 00:55:57,990
No matter how much you loved Pha or how much you hooked up with her,

456
00:55:58,520 --> 00:56:00,010
she died with her mistress anyway.

457
00:56:00,040 --> 00:56:01,830
She still cheated on you in the end, didn't she?

458
00:56:07,570 --> 00:56:08,610
I'm leaving.

459
00:56:09,470 --> 00:56:11,190
My bride-to-be is back.

460
00:56:14,810 --> 00:56:15,550
Let's go.

461
00:56:16,050 --> 00:56:16,670
Sure.
